                    INSTRUCTIONS FOR TELIX 3.15 MOUSE SUPPORT
                              J. S. COOK, 04/02/91

 1. Make sure that the directory containing your mouse driver (MOUSE.COM or
    MOUSE.SYS, CLICK.EXE, and MENU.COM) is in the path statement in your
    AUTOEXEC.BAT file (Example: path c:\;c:\dos;C:\MOUSE).
 2. Add the line "Telix menu 3buttons" to your CLICK.SRC file (without the  
    quotation marks).  If you're not using CLICK.EXE, then just add the line
    "menu Telix.mnu" to a batch file that starts TELIX.EXE.
 3. When you type "Telix", the mouse control and pop-up menu will be
    automatically loaded.
 4. Mouse button designation is as follows:
    a. Left button: ENTER key
    b. Middle button: ESC key
    c. Right button: 1st click displays TELIX COMMAND SUMMARY screen, 2nd
    click displays pop-up menu.
 5. Move the mouse up, down, left, and/or right until the highlighted bar is
    positioned over the command you wish to execute.
 6. Use the left mouse button to make your selection from the pop-up menu.
 7. This mouse control file was compiled using Logitech NEWMENU.EXE Ver. 4.0.
 8. This mouse control file may be distributed freely so long as this docu-
    mentation file is included in the same archive, and nothing has been
    changed in either file.
 9. If you find this file helpful, or if there is another program that you
    wish had mouse support, please drop me a postcard.  There is no fee.
10. If you wish to receive a diskette containing every mouse control file
    that I have developed so far, please include a small donation to cover
    my costs.

